<Layout
	title="Terms of Sale — Buzzyfly"
	description="Terms for buying Buzzyfly digital products, refunds, and license."
	pubDate={new Date('October 22 2026')}
>
	<p>Last updated: October 22, 2026</p>

	<p>
		These terms apply when you buy a product on buzzyfly.com. Questions: support@buzzyfly.com.
	</p>

	<h2>What you are buying</h2>
	<p>
		Access to a web app that runs in your browser on phone or computer. Nothing to download or install. One-time payment. No subscription. No coaching calls. Your access is yours to keep, and it includes any future updates we choose to add to that product. Your client data is saved in your own browser on your own device. We do not receive it.
	</p>

	<h2>Delivery</h2>
	<p>
		After payment is confirmed, the app unlocks on the page you land on after checkout. That page also shows your personal access link. We email the same link as a backup. Open the link on each device you want to use. If you cannot get into the app or lose your link, write support@buzzyfly.com from the checkout address and we will send a fresh one.
	</p>

	<h2>Refunds</h2>
	<p>
		30-day refund if you can't get into the app or it isn't what the listing described. No change-of-mind refunds once you've had access. To ask for one, email support@buzzyfly.com within 30 days of purchase.
	</p>

	<h2>License</h2>
	<p>
		You may use the app and its templates in your own business. You may not resell, republish, or share your access link or the app's content as a product. One purchase, one operator (or the team inside that operator's shop).
	</p>

	<h2>No guarantees beyond the app</h2>
	<p>
		Results depend on how you use the app. We do not promise revenue, client wins, or a specific number of hours saved.
	</p>

	<h2>Limits on our liability</h2>
	<p>
		The app is provided as it is described on the listing. To the extent the law allows, our total liability for any claim about a purchase is limited to the amount you paid for that product. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, such as lost profits, lost clients or lost data. Keep your own backup of any data you rely on, using the app's backup button. Nothing in these terms limits rights you have under consumer law that cannot be excluded.
	</p>

	<h2>Site and law</h2>
	<p>
		We can update these terms. The live page is the current version. If a court finds one line unenforceable, the rest still applies.
	</p>
</Layout>
